# g96-be-tools-b: what the lead applies after the wave

## mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs (hot)
Anchor: the `Worktrees::new(...)` chain, directly after the line
    .with_root_cleanup(Arc::new(crate::worktree_cache_cleanups::CodeGraphCleanup::new(code_graph_cache.clone(), b.tokens.maintenance_io)))
add the line (project_registry is the Arc<Catalog> built earlier in the same function):
    .with_root_cleanup(Arc::new(crate::worktree_cache_cleanups::TrustedRootCleanup::new(project_registry.clone())))
This is `forgetTrustedCodeGraphRoot`: a removed worktree root also leaves the project registry. No Cargo change
(mixdog-workspace and mixdog-scm are already dependencies of mixdog-app-server-daemon).

## Callers that read the new counts (not done here, owned by the session-runtime area)
ExecRuntime::other_owner_shell_work(&ThreadId) -> (foreground, background) in mixdog-tools exec/jobs.rs is the Rust
`otherSessionBackgroundShellJobCount`. The Node caller session-runtime/workspace/transitions.mjs (defaultOwnShellJobCount:
background jobs owned by the sessions that move workspace) has its Rust twin in the workspace transition code; it should
count `jobs.list(owner)` running promoted jobs of the moving sessions (or call the method with each owner) when that code
asks "does a session hold running background shell work". SERVICE_PENDING: no names to remove.
